# hunting-grounds-timing.vrs: hunting-grounds D28 (Session 2, after the restart). hg-timing (a Region location over
# FarbaneWoods, the lock and RegionHunt, two waves of 12 CHAR_Spider_Forest 20 s apart; a group without a spot is skipped, as D4) runs for eleven timing windows
# with Chaos at the pond inside the region, so the lock and the mover both run; -TimingSpan -Windows 10 -MinTracked 10
# reads the budget from the log copy. Then `.nyar purge confirm` while it hunts (D25's purge path) leaves 0 and no
# region line follows. Needs [Debug] TimingLog = true too.
# Needs: the step 3 Release DLL; NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devgo, .devmark, .devhop) and DevChatEcho; the dev events.json
# entries hg-roam, hg-lock, hg-ambush, hg-point, hg-timing (docs/features/HUNTING_GROUNDS.md, Session 2), scope
# FarbaneWoods (the pond is in it, Session 1); [Debug] VerboseLogging = true; Chaos invulnerable
# (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false).
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .devgo pond
expect-log \[DEV TP\] pond
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
mark
chat .nyar event start hg-timing
expect-log event hg-timing started by
expect-log event hg-timing wave 1/2 in [0-9]+ groups? over FarbaneWoods: 12 units queued timeout=30
expect-log event hg-timing wave 2/2 in [0-9]+ groups? over FarbaneWoods: [0-9]+ units queued timeout=60
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units:
shot full hg-timing-start
wait 1500
expect-no-log region (lock|hunt)( hg-timing: (check|move) failed|: (check|move) failing) timeout=3
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units:
mark
chat .nyar purge
wait 2
chat .nyar purge confirm
expect-log purge: 1 events ended, [0-9]+ units queued
expect-no-log region (lock|hunt) hg-timing timeout=15
wait 20
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
